# Cursor AI Rules for Shopify Custom Cursor App

## Code Quality Standards

### General Principles
- Keep code split into small, focused modules and components
- Keep code refactored and DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)
- Follow ReactJS and Shopify best practices
- Maintain Shopify app development standards
- Write clean, readable, and maintainable code

### Task Management for Development
- **Divide work into small, testable, verifiable tasks**
- Complete one task at a time before moving to the next
- On each task completion:
  * Provide a comprehensive summary of what was done
  * Show test results and verification steps
  * Ask for user approval before proceeding to next task
- Each task should be independently testable
- Tasks should have clear success criteria
- Keep tasks focused (avoid combining multiple features in one task)

### React Best Practices
- Use functional components with hooks
- Keep components small and focused (< 300 lines)
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks
- Use proper prop types and validation
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Follow React Context API patterns for global state

### Shopify Standards
- Follow Shopify Polaris design system guidelines
- Use Shopify Polaris components wherever possible
- Follow Remix routing conventions for Shopify apps
- Implement proper authentication and session handling
- Follow Shopify API versioning and deprecation guidelines
- Use Shopify's recommended packages (@shopify/*)

### Code Organization
- Group related files in feature-based folders
- Separate concerns: components, utilities, hooks, contexts
- Use clear and descriptive file and function names
- Keep route files focused on data loading and actions
- Extract business logic into utility functions

### Internationalization (i18n)
- Use @shopify/i18next-shopify for translations
- Keep all user-facing strings in translation files
- Use proper namespace organization for translations
- Support dynamic locale detection
- Provide translations for all supported languages

### Database & Backend
- Use Prisma ORM best practices
- Write efficient database queries
- Handle errors gracefully with proper logging
- Validate all input data
- Use transactions where necessary
- Follow proper data relationships and constraints

### API Development
- Validate all request parameters
- Return consistent JSON response formats
- Use proper HTTP status codes
- Include CORS headers for public endpoints
- Implement proper error handling and logging
- Add caching headers where appropriate
- Consider rate limiting for public APIs

### Testing & Debugging
- Test each feature incrementally before moving forward
- Add proper error logging for debugging
- Use meaningful error messages
- Validate edge cases and error scenarios

### Performance
- Optimize database queries (use select, include wisely)
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders in React
- Use lazy loading where appropriate
- Optimize images and assets

### Security
- Validate and sanitize all user inputs
- Follow Shopify's authentication patterns
- Prevent SQL injection (use Prisma parameterized queries)
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Check for suspicious patterns in public APIs

### Git & Version Control
- Commit frequently with clear, descriptive messages
- Push code after completing each task
- Keep commits atomic and focused
- Document major changes in commit messages

### Documentation
- Add clear comments for complex logic
- Document public APIs and endpoints
- Keep README files up to date
- Document component props and usage
- Create strategy documents for major features

## Project-Specific Rules

### Custom Cursor Feature
- Always include both default and hover cursor states
- Respect hotspot coordinates for cursor positioning
- Handle cursor size scaling properly
- Support mobile detection (disable on mobile if needed)
- Validate cursor image formats and dimensions

### Context Usage
- Use CursorContext for global cursor state
- Avoid prop drilling - use context for deeply nested props
- Keep context providers at appropriate levels
- Use context selectors to prevent unnecessary re-renders

### File Upload
- Validate file types and sizes
- Convert images to data URLs for preview
- Extract image dimensions before upload
- Handle upload errors gracefully
- Provide clear user feedback during upload

### Storefront Integration
- Follow Theme App Extension best practices
- Use App Embed Blocks for easy merchant control
- Implement proper CSS isolation
- Handle conflicts with existing store themes
- Test across different themes and browsers

